From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 03:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: take a group addressed deauth from any link of the AP MLD

ieee80211_prepare_and_rx_handle() translates the link addresses of an
individually addressed frame to MLD addresses, but leaves a group
addressed frame as it is. A group addressed Deauthentication or
Disassociation frame from an AP affiliated with the AP MLD therefore
names that AP's link address as the BSSID. ieee80211_rx_mgmt_deauth()
and ieee80211_rx_mgmt_disassoc() compare the BSSID with the AP MLD
address alone and drop the frame without a trace, unless the link
address of that AP equals the AP MLD address. cfg80211 would drop it
as well, as it compares the BSSID with the connected address.

Deauthentication frames may be sent as group addressed frames
(802.11-2024 12.3.3.1), and the destination deauthenticates with the
originating MLD (802.11be 11.3.4.5). An AP that restarts a link
flushes its stations and sends such a frame; a non-AP MLD associated
on another link then keeps a dead association.

Name the sender of a group addressed deauthentication or disassociation
frame by the AP MLD address when it comes from the BSSID of the link it
was received on. The frame has passed the management frame protection
checks at that point.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/net/mac80211/mlme.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
@@ -5678,6 +5678,27 @@ const char *ieee80211_get_reason_code_st
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * ieee80211_prepare_and_rx_handle() translates the addresses of
+ * individually addressed frames only.
+ */
+static void ieee80211_mgd_group_addrs_to_mld(struct ieee80211_link_data *link,
+					     struct ieee80211_mgmt *mgmt)
+{
+	struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata = link->sdata;
+
+	if (!ieee80211_vif_is_mld(&sdata->vif) ||
+	    !is_multicast_ether_addr(mgmt->da))
+		return;
+
+	if (!ether_addr_equal(mgmt->bssid, link->u.mgd.bssid) ||
+	    !ether_addr_equal(mgmt->sa, link->u.mgd.bssid))
+		return;
+
+	ether_addr_copy(mgmt->sa, sdata->vif.cfg.ap_addr);
+	ether_addr_copy(mgmt->bssid, sdata->vif.cfg.ap_addr);
+}
+
 static void ieee80211_rx_mgmt_deauth(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 				     struct ieee80211_mgmt *mgmt, size_t len)
 {
@@ -11845,9 +11866,11 @@ void ieee80211_sta_rx_queued_frame(struc
 		ieee80211_rx_mgmt_auth(sdata, mgmt, skb->len);
 		break;
 	case IEEE80211_STYPE_DEAUTH:
+		ieee80211_mgd_group_addrs_to_mld(link, mgmt);
 		ieee80211_rx_mgmt_deauth(sdata, mgmt, skb->len);
 		break;
 	case IEEE80211_STYPE_DISASSOC:
+		ieee80211_mgd_group_addrs_to_mld(link, mgmt);
 		ieee80211_rx_mgmt_disassoc(sdata, mgmt, skb->len);
 		break;
 	case IEEE80211_STYPE_ASSOC_RESP:
